  "reason": "R6 is strong near-direct anticipation: in a BCC refractory WVTaTi alloy, increasing Cr causes precipitation of a network-distributed Cr2Ta Laves phase, closely matching Cr addition and the reticulated Cr-rich Laves mediator in the later HfMoTaTiZr alloy. The remaining records supply complementary principles: alloying-induced lattice distortion or dislocation strengthening, second-phase strengthening, and control of phase continuity or precipitate morphology to balance strength and plasticity. In particular, R3 shows that a continuous ductile BCC matrix with a suitably distributed ordered second phase can improve the strength-ductility balance, while R2 supplies the counterpoint that uncontrolled grain-boundary Laves phases are brittle. Together, these records could plausibly lead an expert to test a limited Cr addition in HfMoTaTiZr and seek an interconnected but crack-deflecting Laves morphology, even though the exact 4.2 at.% optimum and measured improvements were not disclosed."
